{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795616215,"nonce":"k5HAN5gBKQ3BH2pObVo651IMicQ=","title":"Compile CN_STYLES and UA_STYLES from Sass sources at build time","message":"cn_styles.rs is 2,360 lines and ua_styles.rs 347, each one `concat!` of a raw string inside `@layer components`. The sheets repeat themselves: about 120 `var(--ease-*)` and 119 `var(--duration-*)` uses (the same `transition:` shapes), 83 `var(--radius-*)`, 31 `color-mix` tints for hover and press, 34 `@keyframes`, and the same size and disabled variants per component. The pieces cannot be split into files, shared or checked. Plan: write them as SCSS, compile at build time, keep `CN_STYLES` and `UA_STYLES` as the same `\u0026str` constants.\n\nDecision\n- SCSS through `grass` (pure Rust, no node, no C++). Not Less: no maintained Rust compiler. Not a proc macro: it cannot track the files it reads on stable, so edits would not rebuild. Not committed CSS output: it drifts from its source.\n- A `build.rs` in blinc_cn and blinc_layout compiles `styles/index.scss` into `OUT_DIR`, and `pub const CN_STYLES: \u0026str = include_str!(concat!(env!(\"OUT_DIR\"), \"/cn.css\"))`. `cargo:rerun-if-changed=styles` covers every partial.\n- Shared mixins and functions live in a small build-dependency crate (`blinc_sass`) that holds the compile helper and the shared partials, served to grass through its `Fs` trait. blinc_cn is published apart from blinc_layout, so it cannot read a path in the other crate.\n- Applications keep writing plain CSS. Nothing is compiled at run time.\n\nWhat the mixins should cover\n- `transition($props...)` from the duration and easing tokens.\n- A state layer: hover and press tints with `color-mix`, plus focus ring and disabled.\n- Size and variant sets generated from maps with `@each`, in place of one hand-written block per size.\n- `overflow-fade`, the corner and shadow tokens, and the `@keyframes` pairs for enter and exit.\n\nConstraints to check in the spike\n- Blinc's dialect must pass through untouched: `overflow-fade`, `corner-shape`, `@flow`, pointer queries, `color-mix(in srgb, ...)`, `var(--a, var(--b))`, `calc()`, attribute selectors, `:not(:disabled)`, percent keyframes. Sass may rewrite `calc` and colour functions.\n- `@layer components { ... }` wraps everything. `@use` must come first, so the wrapper goes in the entry through an `@include` or in `build.rs`.\n- Diagnostics: grass reports file and line for Sass errors but has no source maps. `build.rs` should also run blinc_css's diagnostic parser on the compiled sheet and fail the build on an invalid value, naming the partial where it can (a debug build may emit `/* partial:line */` markers).\n- The web catalog reads `cn_styles.rs` and `ua_styles.rs` by path for the preview digest (tools/build-web-examples catalog `mod.rs` and `build.rs`) and cuts per-component excerpts from the compiled text. Digest every `styles/**/*.scss`, and read the compiled sheet for excerpts.\n- Windows checkouts: no partial named `aux`, `con`, `prn`, `nul`, `com1`-`com9` or `lpt1`-`lpt9`.\n- Build cost and platforms: measure grass on the whole sheet; `build.rs` runs on the host for wasm, Android and iOS. Check MSRV 1.85 and licence (`deny.toml`). `cargo publish` must include `styles/`. Refresh `ci/workspace.lock` with `scripts/ci-refresh-lock.sh`.\n\nPhases\n0. Spike: compile today's CSS unchanged as SCSS; compare to the original rule by rule; time it; list what grass rewrites.\n1. `blinc_sass` and the build scripts; `CN_STYLES` is unchanged in content. Tests: the sheet parses; a stored digest of the compiled text.\n2. Split cn_styles into one partial per component, a 1:1 move. The compiled text is identical but for whitespace.\n3. Introduce the mixins and maps and remove the duplication. Each step shows its compiled diff, which must change no rule that a recorder test or golden reads, except on purpose.\n4. The same for ua_styles.\n5. Tooling and docs: the catalog digest and excerpts, a contributing page on writing component styles, the CHANGELOGs.\n\nDone when\n- `CN_STYLES` and `UA_STYLES` come from `styles/` and no `.rs` file holds CSS.\n- All recorder, layout and cn tests and goldens pass, and the previews digest passes the docs workflow.\n- The largest partial is under 400 lines.\n\nOpen\n- Whether to publish `blinc_sass` for application authors. Later, and only if wanted.\n- Whether a token file (`_tokens.scss`) should also generate the theme's variable names, so the Rust theme and the sheet share one list.","files":null}]}